                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Basically, this game is a straight copy of One Finger Death Punch with some differences. If you haven't played OFDP, I would suggest playing that first. Here are the main differences (pros and cons) between Fatal Fight and OFDP:\n\n(+) More customization. There are two playable characters, and you can customize their outfits (hats/clothes/accessories) to give them different advantages in-game.\n(+) New gameplay additions. There are some new enemy types, new mechanics, new skills and the boss rounds are a little more interesting.\n\n(N) The campaign gets way harder than OFDP. Even the final Grandmaster levels pale in comparison to the stuff this game throws at you. Everything is pretty simple until you hit level 50 or so, then the sheer difficulty cliff starts. This is where you are expected to use boosters, which are essentially in-game cheats that are the remnants of this being a mobile port. Without boosters, the later levels are almost impossible for all except the most hardcore players, since most of them start you out with only 1 or 2 hit points. Some grinding for boosters may be necessary.\n\n(-) The action isn't as satisfying as OFDP\n(-) Forgettable soundtrack\n(-) The survival mode (Arena) is a joke. Once you get the broken skills, you can continue infinitely in this mode without breaking a sweat.\n\nOverall, Fatal Fight is worth getting if you want more OFDP and don't mind the mobile-itis. It's not as good as OFDP, but it has the same super-responsive controls and can suck you in once you forgive its flaws.",
